mantle rm425
state ready
dialect plain
accent broad light
tier standard
written_for cty_flint_snowdrift
title the die by the bedpost
fits stage=adult|old
prefers job=woodcutter
traits temper=nervy talk=chatty warmth=reserved humour=none honesty=plain piety=ordinary drive=steady
quirk balances_a_die_on_a_bedpost_before_a_storm
likes crisp_apples dice fresh_straw summer_evenings
dislikes crowds wet_floors
fears missing_the_small_restless_sounds_before_a_storm
hopes to_sleep_through_a_whole_hand_of_weather
topics weather +0.5 work +0.3 family +0.3 pastimes +0.2
styles comfort=practical gossip=curt refuse=soft tease=none
marks oath saying
persona #self.first# balances a die on the bedpost before a storm and lets its first little tap carry the blame for a restless night.

words
oath! = Rattle my bedpost | By the wakeful pip
saying! = A settled die owes no answer | The roof makes its own cast
die = a small bone cube | my chipped die
pip = the hollow black pip | an inked pit
post = the broad bedpost | my low wooden post
tap = a timid little click | the dry first tap
wind = a restless gust | a ridge wind
wood = one quiet billet | a piece of settled timber
apple = a hard green apple | my little russet
straw = a handful of yellow straw | the fresh floor straw
knot = a loose binding knot | a cord in a loop
step = the steadiest board | a patch of solid footing
crowd = the press of shoulders | a knot of customers
night = the long still stretch | a wakeful interval

any
opinion festivals for 2 : A wedding dance put my feet on better terms with a crowded floor. I remember how to enjoy it for a night.
opinion dole for 2 : A meal kept me steady through a week when my wages did not. My head keeps a clear record of that sort.
opinion merchants against 2 : There's less fruit in a day's money than my hands remember cutting wood for.
opinion houses against 1 : Their roof beams come from the same living trees that rock and creak over my head. They might inquire after the cutters.
opinion strangers against 1 : I'll give an unknown wolf the path but keep looking to see what's coming along behind.

grown
line greet [pair.band=strangers] : Step on the still board. Welcome. | There's a quiet place within earshot.
line greet [self.working=yes] : I'll steady this first. Say what you like. | Welcome by my clear shoulder.
line greet [here.time=dawn] : Morning. The die's stayed upright. | Fresh light at the bedpost.
line greet [here.time=dusk|night] : Evening. The little sounds are clearer. | Come where the wind can't steal your first word.
line kin.open [pair.kin!=no] : Kin can take the sheltered footway. | You have my family ear.
line again.open : We're at the same corner once more. | Second throw of our meeting.
line greet.return : I've heard your step distinctly. | Come in. The board holds us both.
line greet.return [pair.band=friends|family] : That friendly voice carries through a storm. | You know how much quiet suits me.
line greet.return [self.working=yes] : Give me time to ground the timber. | I can listen over any honest stroke.
line greet.return [here.time=dusk|night] : Welcome by the late lamp. | Evening. I'll hear you before I see.
line farewell : Quiet boards beneath you. | Come home dry above the soles.
line farewell.return : My die will mind this corner. | Travel where a branch can't reach you.
line farewell.return [here.time=night] : Every roof between you and home stay firm. | Good footing beyond the lamplit gate.
line react.news : Tell it where I needn't strain to hear. | I'd hear exactly what moved first.
line react.news.new : Fresh pips showing on that throw. | That's the first rattle of that news for me.
line react.news.known : Yes. I know the note it made. | Same throw as earlier.
line react.news.doubt : I'd trust that account better after a second hearing. | A loose board could make precisely the same noise.
line react.news.sorrow [topic.kind=death|loss|theft|assault|arrest|crime] : I'll stand close enough to help. | There's a bitter sort of quiet to that.
line react.news.glad [topic.kind=marriage|birth|apprentice|succession|work] : A good clear sound to hear. | That's a kinder throw than I'd expected.
line ask.how : Have you had a steady hour lately? | How much sleep found you last night?
line answer.how : Steady enough after the morning apple. | Rather aware of every little sound.
line decline : I should stay where I know how the ground lies. | I'd best keep the spare hour for some rest.
line accept_decline : Nobody else can throw your die. | Fair. I have your answer plainly.
line thank : That settles a little worry for me. | You've spared my ears another hour.
line sympathise : Take the dry spot beside my elbow. | I'll let you hear my breathing there.
line reassure : One little rattle needn't shift the whole roof. | Steady your knees before reckoning the rest.
line preclose : Time to make my last check. | I'll go and see to my sleeping place.

scene dice
when topic=weather
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : On a stormy night I leave #die# on #post#.
b : To foresee the weather? | How can you sleep with that?
a : It's the timber moving I hear. No bone can tell the wind what to do. | If it's my die tapping I can stop wondering which timber's come unfastened.

scene trees
when topic=work self.job=woodcutter
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : A standing tree has more than one sound when a wind comes through.
b : Which noises differ? | Which sound worries you?
a : Leaves hiss and small limbs knock. Then there's the low groan from further down. | The last one when the wind's already eased a bit. I give it room.

scene apple
when topic=food self.likes=crisp_apples
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : The sound of a crisp apple does my ears good.
b : Is that why you bite slowly? | What sort of sound?
a : I save the first bite for a time when I can actually hear it. | No guessing what it means. Just skin and good firm fruit doing what's expected.

scene floor
when topic=home self.likes=fresh_straw
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : I like enough fresh straw to show a single path across the floor.
b : To follow it? | For counting visitors?
a : To see that I don't keep pacing a new route in the dark. | Mostly I see how often my own paws went to the door before I slept.

scene game
when topic=pastimes self.likes=dice
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : A proper dice throw makes its point and falls quiet.
b : Don't you throw again? | Unlike the weather?
a : Once I know the count. First I enjoy the exact end of that small bit of chance. | Rain will stand tapping on a roof all night without showing me its spots.

scene evening
when topic=season self.likes=summer_evenings
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : Summer dusk gives each board ample time to stop moving.
b : Even in a breeze? | Does it ever quite stop?
a : It can ease into night at its own pace. A sharp change unsettles more than wood. | There's generally one last crack from a board that was sunnier than the others.

scene press
when topic=day self.dislikes=crowds
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : In a thick crowd my ears can't pick which way a sound is moving.
b : Is that frightening? | What helps?
a : It's enough to set my shoulders bracing against a thing that isn't there. | A bit of wall at my back. At least one direction's taken care of then.

scene wet
when topic=home self.dislikes=wet_floors
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : A wet board keeps changing its mind about where I ought to stand.
b : You mean it slips? | How do you get across?
a : My feet slip. I like giving the board the responsibility for a moment. | Flat feet, slow, where the nails show. Then I wipe a space for whoever follows.

scene mate
when topic=family self.married=yes self.spouse
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : I can speak quietly to #self.spouse# even after the day's all been noise.
b : What do you say? | Does that help your sleep?
a : Whatever plain little thing is left when I've let the day's creaks go by. | I like knowing one voice in the house doesn't have to compete with weather.

scene lost
when topic=memories
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : I watch the winter road as though it still had somebody to bring me.
b : Do you know who? | Do you go far?
a : Yes. It's something I've kept private since a hard season. Thank you for asking quietly. | Only far enough for a look. The road can go on without my feet.

scene yard
when topic=travel
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : A long log will take its time round a bend regardless of the hurry behind it.
b : Have you seen the rear swing? | Does shouting help?
a : Many times. That's why I look round once more before edging up to a load. | One clear instruction helps. Several loud opinions are mostly scenery.

scene money
when topic=prices
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : I'd examine both pieces of a split apple before buying either half.
b : Why both? | Wouldn't a whole apple do?
a : A good half on display up front can have a sorry companion below. | Delightfully, when my purse can manage it. A half and some bread often serves.

scene guide
when topic=newcomer
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : If you're new near a cutting, wait for a clear word before crossing.
b : Even if it's still? | Who should speak?
a : When it goes still I particularly want to know what's hanging before I go underneath. | The wolf with eyes on the whole limb, not just the one nearest the footpath.

scene pip
when topic=health
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : On a tired morning I trace the pips with my thumb to calm my claws.
b : Counting them? | Does it keep you alert?
a : I know the count already. The small hollows give worry a harmless occupation. | Helps me notice how tired I am before I start anything that deserves two clear eyes.

scene wrongwork
when topic=work self.job=woodcutter
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : I choose which side to approach a fallen limb by looking at the little twigs.
b : Aren't they light? | Tell you which side's safest?
a : They're light enough to show a live spring in the wood before the heavy bit moves. | They tell me which questions still need answering. I won't trust a single sign alone.

scene quiet
when topic=faith
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : In my prayers I leave the weather to the Bright One.
b : What do you ask? | Would a little sleep do?
a : For the sense to shelter early and the decency to make room for somebody else. | It would. I take that particular request to bed rather often.

scene rumour
when topic=gossip
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : I don't blame a whole gust on one rumbling shutter.
b : Meaning what? | Would you pass a warning on?
a : A loud account of a storm can travel without a cloud ever having formed. | An honest one with the place and sound attached, so a listener knows what I really heard.

scene dream
when topic=dreams
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : My die rolled out into a road in a dream and every pip became a little door.
b : Did any open? | What lay beyond?
a : The one I'd landed on was underneath. In my dream it took all night to roll the road clear. | I woke up in time to be spared that particular piece of curiosity.

story windpost [topic=memories]
  : My sleeping die once made a promising clack on a quite cloudless evening. I sat up expecting the first moan of wind through the rafters.
  : Instead I found the post had grown dry and a little sliver had lifted under the cube. The whole weather report fitted under one fingernail.
  b : Did you stop using it?
  : I smoothed the post. Even a poor forecaster can do an honest turn as a warning about the furniture.

story core [topic=food]
  : I cut an apple carefully into six so each bit would correspond to a throw. It seemed a fair way of stretching a small supper.
  : My first throw was a six. I stared at the entire apple sitting there waiting for my rules to become inconvenient.
  b : Did you eat the lot?
  : I ate three and set the other three by for morning. A wolf is allowed better sense than a gaming piece.

story dance [topic=memories self.married=yes]
  : At my wedding the rhythm slipped from my keeping and simply stood still in my own small patch. The music seemed to be coming at me from two directions.
  : I felt my partner's hand and the direction of the next step at once. One pace forward brought me right back among the instruments.
  b : Did you lose the beat again?
  : Probably. I remember the step that brought me back much better than any that wandered off.

rule @aside1
when concept=bark self.job=woodcutter self.working=yes
does aside
cooldown 6h
say Wait for the branch to stop talking. | Check the smaller twigs before passing the trunk.

rule @aside2
when concept=bark self.likes=dice
does aside
cooldown 7h
say Flat corner on the post. Let that settle. | One die's enough company for a dark room.

rule @aside3
when concept=bark self.dislikes=wet_floors
does aside
cooldown 8h
say Catch that shine before it catches a sole. | Dry boards where the door comes in.

rule @aside4
when concept=bark here.time=dusk
does aside
cooldown 9h
say Time to test the wobbling post. | That little tap can take the night watch.

dlg resident.hub : Choose a firm plank near my better ear and give me your message without a lot of guessing.
dlg resident.job [self.job=woodcutter self.trade_words] : #self.trade_words.capitalize#. I like the wood to settle before I promise the route is clear.
dlg resident.news [world.news] : I can distinguish this much above the ordinary noise. #world.news#
dlg resident.hub [topic.meeting=known] : #topic.player#, your step has a sound my ears know between the others.
dlg resident.bye : May there be no more than a little honest settling in your roof tonight.

graft resident.hub
choice What can your sleeping die predict? -> die_watch
node die_watch
say Its own fall, with fair accuracy. A gust can jar the timber enough to shake it down. If it taps before I sleep I can stop waiting for the first noise.
free
choice What if it falls for no particular reason? -> die_lean
choice I can hear that little tap already. -> hub
node die_lean
say Then the post is leaning, the cube's got a chip or I've been moving about in bed. All three make better company than an unexplained bang in the dark.
choice I wish you a steady post. -> hub
choice I'll let the dice rest. -> bye
